    "title": "Dakota Johnson's daring sheer gala look has everyone asking: Too much or just enough? [See Photos] - NewsBreak",
    "text": "10 hours ago Dakota Johnson commanded attention in a daring sheer gown at a high-profile charity gala in New York, where she joined fellow stars in support of the Kering Foundation’s Caring for Women dinner. The actress, 35, best known for her breakout role in the Fifty Shades of Grey franchise, arrived in a floor-length black Gucci dress with lace panels that revealed much of her figure.\n© REX Features/Shutterstock /The Grosby Group Dakota Johnson attends the 4th Annual Kering Foundation Caring for Women Dinner, New York. She paired the look with a matching bra-and-underwear set, styled her hair in a sleek updo, and finished the ensemble with a tennis necklace and silver earrings.\nThe Manhattan event drew a host of other celebrities. Lauren Sánchez Bezos made her first red carpet appearance since marrying Amazon founder Jeff Bezos in June, while Colman Domingo, Demi Moore , and Adrien Brody were also photographed in designer couture.\n© Backgrid/The Grosby Group © Instar Images/The Grosby Group Johnson’s striking fashion choice follows a series of bold style moments in recent weeks. In August, she was spotted in New York wearing a black sheer midi dress with long sleeves.\nSpeaking to Etalk on August 20, Johnson admitted she’s more hesitant when it comes to switching up her hairstyle. “I’m like obviously physically attached to my hair, but I’m very emotionally attached to it,” she said. “I should probably change things up, but I don’t think I will.\n© Splash News/The Grosby Group She also revealed she has no plans to step away from the romance genre. Johnson is set to appear in Verity, the screen adaptation of Colleen Hoover’s bestselling novel. \"I’m just so interested in love and love stories,” she explained. “It’s so much a part of our human development and our journey.”\nBorn in Austin, Texas, in 1989 to actors Don Johnson and Melanie Griffith , Dakota grew up in a Hollywood family before pursuing her own acting career. She went on to star in films including Suspiria , The Lost Daughter, and Cha Cha Real Smooth . Alongside acting, she co-founded the production company TeaTime Pictures in 2019.\n© REX Features/Shutterstock /The Grosby Group 40",
